    <comment>Based on the digitization of the error bars from the figures, the authors considered 1sigma = 5.136% experimental error for all data points based on the uncertainty analysis in the Supp. Mat. (Table S3, yellow-highlighted value). Therefore, constant relative error model was assumed when using Minimal Spline Fit. Note that this 5.136% relative error is in very good agreement with the recommended typical 1sigma error (5%) for HDC measurements by Zhang et al. (https://doi.org/10.1016/j.combustflame.2021.111867).</comment>
